  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 section to `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, dated 2026-10-20 to match `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE`. It sits above v2.3.0 and uses the same format.\n\n```markdown\n## v2.4.0 (2026-10-20)\n\n### Breaking changes\n- The deprecated `--legacy` flag has been removed from `sync`. [ACME-421] (thanks @mira)\n\n### Features\n- The `report` command can now export to CSV. [ACME-412] (thanks @mira)\n- Uploads are now retried with backoff when the server returns a 503. [ACME-415] (thanks @jonas)\n\n### Fixes\n- An empty config file no longer causes a crash. [ACME-419] (thanks @tom)\n- Monthly summary totals are now correct for leap years. [ACME-423] (thanks @priya)\n```\n\n**Decision needed on the version number:** ACME-421 is marked `!` because it removes the `--legacy` flag. That's a breaking change, but `VERSION` only goes up to the next minor version (2.4.0). If you follow semantic versioning, this release should be 3.0.0. I left `VERSION` and the heading at 2.4.0. If you want 3.0.0, I'll update both. If you keep 2.4.0, you could add a short migration note to the breaking-change entry telling users what to do instead of using `--legacy`.\n\nI also listed ACME-415 (retrying uploads) as a feature rather than a fix. Move it to Fixes if you see it differently.",
